api.doc:
How to round a value that falls between two candidates. The `Half` modes only differ on
exact ties; the others look only at whether anything is discarded.
`HalfUp` ties toward +infinity (2.5 to 3, -2.5 to -2); `HalfDown` ties toward -infinity;
`HalfEven` ties to the even neighbour (banker's rounding); `HalfAwayFromZero` ties away from
zero (school rounding, Java's HALF_UP); `HalfTowardZero` ties toward zero (Java's HALF_DOWN);
`Up` rounds away from zero; `Down` toward zero (truncation); `Ceiling` toward +infinity;
`Floor` toward -infinity.
